# The theme data files are hand-aligned on purpose: a palette reads as columns,
# and one `= "#rrggbb", -- name` per aligned row is the whole point. stylua
# collapses that alignment (it has no concept of it), so formatting them would
# be a readability regression, not a cleanup.
#
# hyprland.lua is CODE and is deliberately NOT ignored — it stays stylua-clean
# and CI enforces that. This split is why .stylua.toml exists at all: to keep
# an editor's format-on-save from retabbing the files it does touch.
themes/*/theme.lua
themes/*/nvim.lua
themes/*/wezterm/colors.lua
